1. Time-Series EDA 
    1. Rolling Statistics 
        Smooth out short-term fluctuations and highlight longer-term trends
        a. Rolling Mean / Moving Average 
        
            df['rolling_mean_7'] = df['value'].rolling(window=7).mean()

        b. Rolling Variance / Std Dev (to detect volatility)

            df['rolling_std_7'] = df['value'].rolling(window=7).std()

    2. Seasonal Decomposition 
        Break down time series into trend, seasonality, and residuals 
            Trend -> long-term direction (eg increasing patient visits)
            seasonality -> repeating cycles (eg monthly billiing cycles, yearly flu season)
            Residuals -> irregular noise

    3. Helper Functions for seasonal EDA 
        see .py file

    4. Visualization
        Line plots for raw + rolling mean 
        Decomposition plots for trend/seasonality
        Heatmaps for seasonal patterns (eg month vs year)
